  "description": "Application for Full Planning Permission for the installation of a single storey independent garden room building within the rear garden and within the curtilage of the premises owned by the Planning Applicant, at Flat 2, 124 Highbury New Park, London N5 2DR. \n\nThe proposed garden room will provide ancillary space to enable home office working, and additional living space for the applicants and their new family, whilst maintaining the majority of the current garden space. Providing the proposed garden room will enable the owners and their growing family to remain within the borough and continue to contribute the local economy, support local business, public amenities, and schools. \n\nThe proposed building is appropriate in scale to the existing building and the surrounding properties, occupying a modest proportion of the existing garden, having an overall footprint of 4.300m x 2.600m within a garden footprint of 9.8m x 7.7m.\n\nThe applicants own a long leasehold interest in the premises, with an unexpired term of 105 years.\n\nFormal Landlord’s consent has been received for the proposed garden room.\n",
